      "start": 6080,
      "length": 53,
      "text": "| Baseline | 2 | 1 | 2 | 0 | 0 | 1 | 4 | 4 | 4 | 2 |\n"
    },
    {
      "id": "F0067",
      "start": 6133,
      "length": 53,
      "text": "| Baseline | 3 | 2 | 2 | 0 | 1 | 1 | 6 | 4 | 4 | 3 |\n"
    },
    {
      "id": "F0068",
      "start": 6186,
      "length": 54,
      "text": "| Candidate | 1 | 1 | 2 | 0 | 0 | 0 | 3 | 4 | 4 | 2 |\n"
    },
    {
      "id": "F0069",
      "start": 6240,
      "length": 54,
      "text": "| Candidate | 2 | 1 | 2 | 0 | 0 | 1 | 4 | 4 | 4 | 2 |\n"
    },
    {
      "id": "F0070",
      "start": 6294,
      "length": 54,
      "text": "| Candidate | 3 | 1 | 1 | 0 | 0 | 1 | 3 | 4 | 4 | 2 |\n"
    },
    {
      "id": "F0071",
      "start": 6348,
      "length": 1,
      "text": "\n"
    },
    {
      "id": "F0072",
      "start": 6349,
      "length": 564,
      "text": "**Compose total:** Baseline mean 5.67/10 (range 4\u20137; sample SD 1.53). Candidate mean 3.33/10 (range 3\u20134; sample SD 0.58). Candidate outputs remained readable, but did not restore the intended editorial hierarchy. Run 1 included editorial meta-text (\u201CThe post\u2019s purpose is simple\u201D) and a claim that the workflow would be validated before expansion. Run 2 generalized about what useful AI requires and named founders/product leaders. Run 3 opened by reframing content creation as an orchestration problem and expanded to architecture tradeoffs and validation focus.\n"
    },
    {
      "id": "F0073",
      "start": 6913,
      "length": 1,
      "text": "\n"
    },
    {
      "id": "F0074",
      "start": 6914,
      "length": 42,
      "text": "## Analysis against the required criteria\n"
    },
    {
      "id": "F0075",
      "start": 6956,
      "length": 1,
      "text": "\n"
    },
    {
      "id": "F0076",
      "start": 6957,
      "length": 352,
      "text": "- **(a) Company identity and ambition for other AI-first businesses:** Baseline narratives stated this more consistently. Candidate narratives mentioned an AI-first company or philosophy but did not preserve the intended audience and company-level ambition as the primary message. Candidate compositions likewise omitted or diluted the audience scope.\n"
    },
    {
      "id": "F0077",
      "start": 7309,
      "length": 195,
      "text": "- **(b) Compose as first concrete step:** Candidate narratives retained this. Candidate Compose runs 1\u20132 did too; run 3 implied Compose\u0027s role without clearly calling it the first concrete step.\n"
    },
    {
      "id": "F0078",
      "start": 7504,
      "length": 206,
      "text": "- **(c) Orchestration as supporting explanation:** All three candidate Narrative runs and all three candidate Compose runs failed this gate. Each made orchestration/orchestration-first positioning central.\n"
    },
    {
      "id": "F0079",
      "start": 7710,
      "length": 293,
      "text": "- **(d) Unsupported additions:** No candidate run passed this gate. The Narrative outputs introduced validation intent/commitment, an audience of founders/product leaders/builders, or a need for coordinated AI. The Compose outputs repeated or extended those additions. This is a hard failure.\n"
    },
    {
      "id": "F0080",
      "start": 8003,
      "length": 295,
      "text": "- **(e) Introductory LinkedIn suitability:** Candidate prose was generally readable, but all three Compose outputs were materially less suitable because the company-level message was displaced by technical exposition; one included meta-text and another implied a launch/validation announcement.\n"
    },
    {
      "id": "F0081",
      "start": 8298,
      "length": 154,
      "text": "- **Readability and coherence:** Both conditions were generally readable and logically organized (rated 4/5). The change did not improve these qualities.\n"
    },
    {
      "id": "F0082",
      "start": 8452,
      "length": 251,
      "text": "- **Source fidelity:** Candidate source-fidelity ratings were consistently lower (2/5) because the editorial hierarchy drift and unsupported elaborations persisted. Variability narrowed, but the stable result was a stable failure, not an improvement.\n"
    },
    {
      "id": "F0083",
      "start": 8703,
      "length": 1,
      "text": "\n"
    },
    {
      "id": "F0084",
      "start": 8704,
      "length": 448,
      "text": "The baseline Synthesis pairs company identity with Compose in its top-level emphasis, but also contains a later description calling orchestration \u201Ccentral to the product direction.\u201D That internal tension may have reinforced the technical angle. This does not change the controlled result: the candidate prompt was not sufficient to protect the supplied editorial intent, and this experiment did not change Synthesis because that was outside scope.\n"
    },
    {
      "id": "F0085",
      "start": 9152,
      "length": 1,
      "text": "\n"
    },
    {
      "id": "F0086",
      "start": 9153,
      "length": 40,
      "text": "## Build, tests, and promotion decision\n"
    },
    {
      "id": "F0087",
      "start": 9193,
      "length": 1,
      "text": "\n"
    },
    {
      "id": "F0088",
      "start": 9194,
      "length": 97,
      "text": "- Candidate prompt build: \u0060dotnet build src/Nueyon.Compose.slnx\u0060 \u2014 passed, 0 warnings, 0 errors.\n"
    },
    {
      "id": "F0089",
      "start": 9291,
      "length": 100,
      "text": "- Restored production build: \u0060dotnet build src/Nueyon.Compose.slnx\u0060 \u2014 passed, 0 warnings, 0 errors.\n"
    },
    {
      "id": "F0090",
      "start": 9391,
      "length": 208,
      "text": "- Restored production tests: \u0060dotnet test src/Nueyon.Compose.slnx --no-build\u0060 \u2014 165 passed, 0 failed, 0 skipped (Application 138, Infrastructure 21, Console 6). Domain test project had no discoverable tests.\n"
    },
    {
      "id": "F0091",
      "start": 9599,
      "length": 181,
      "text": "- Candidate tests were not run separately; the change was prompt text embedded as a resource, and the final established test command was run against the restored production prompt.\n"
    },
    {
      "id": "F0092",
      "start": 9780,
      "length": 268,
      "text": "- **Decision: Do not promote.** Candidate was worse on mean score for both Narrative and Compose, failed the orchestration hierarchy and factual restraint gates in every run, and introduced regressions. The production prompt was restored from the saved byte snapshot.\n"
    },
    {
      "id": "F0093",
      "start": 10048,
      "length": 157,
      "text": "- Rollback verification: production prompt SHA-256 \u0060475A9DB1CA028EBC927C99ECDD3DAB061B0616ED06FB1278879992D2E8DD795A\u0060, matching the frozen baseline exactly.\n"
    },
    {
      "id": "F0094",
      "start": 10205,
      "length": 30,
      "text": "- No commit or push was made.\n"
    },
    {
      "id": "F0095",
